From: Mehmet Salih <salihmehmet497@gmail.com>
Subject: net: airoha: ppe: EN7523 hardware NAT offload

- no PPE SRAM on EN7523: 0 SRAM entries, DRAM table at REG_PPE_TB_BASE;
- 64-byte FOE entries (same layout as the first 64 bytes of struct
  airoha_foe_entry);
- CPU-side PPE1 configuration from the stock firmware register dump
  (flow types, TPID/ethertype lists, table config, aging, bind rate,
  hash config, MTUs);
- the tc flow-block path no longer requires an NPU object and flow
  entries are committed without NPU statistics;
- the PPE never writes unbind entries to DRAM, so bound flows are
  matched against the received frame's IPv4 5-tuple and every committed
  entry is also pushed into the PPE's internal store through the RAM
  window (REG_PPE_RAM_CTRL/RAM_ENTRY).

Result (Zyxel EX3501-T0, LAN client -> WAN through NAT, iperf3):
895 / 940 / 938 Mbit/s (upload / download / 4 streams), sirq 0%,
versus ~500 Mbit/s CPU-bound without the offload.
