+/* EN7523 (hypothesis 34): CPU-side PPE1 table configuration.  Values come
+ * from vendor hw_nat.ko init_module()/PpeSetFoeEbl() (non HIR-10/12 path)
+ * and from the live register dump of the stock firmware:
+ * - REG_PPE_PPE_FLOW_CFG: IPv4 NAT/NAPT/frag, IPv6 3T/5T, L2 bridge, hash
+ *   options -- with this register at 0 the PPE reported NO_FLOW (0x07) for
+ *   every packet, TCP included (verified live on the Zyxel EX3501-T0).
+ * - REG_PPE_TB_CFG: classic layout, table size code in bits 2..0 (4 = 16K
+ *   entries), search-miss 3 (forward to CPU and build entry), aging
+ *   enabled for non-L4/unbind/TCP/UDP/TCP-FIN, keepalive off, hash mode 0.
+ *   Bits above 15 are left at their reset value.
+ * - Unbind age 1000 packets / 3 s, bind age 60 s (TCP-FIN 1 s), bind
+ *   limits 4000/4000/8000, bind rate 30 (vendor PpeSetBindThreshold).
+ * - REG_PPE_GLO_CFG = 0x00038743, the value the vendor firmware runs with.
+ * Live test with these written via /dev/mem: CRSN changed from NO_FLOW to
+ * HIT_UNBIND / HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED with valid FOE indexes.
